Subject: Converter: write tie_word_embeddings = True

update_config() writes tie_word_embeddings = True instead of False. The deployed engine predates upstream
commit 8962e94 ("Conversion: Fix incorrect config update during compile"), so this reverts its effect. Only the
config.json written by convert.py is affected; loading and serving are not. Kept so that the patched tree is
byte-identical to the deployed engine. Drop this patch (and update engine.sha256) if you convert models
with this tree.

diff --git a/exllamav3/conversion/quant_config.py b/exllamav3/conversion/quant_config.py
index 51843ec..c391d5e 100644
--- a/exllamav3/conversion/quant_config.py
+++ b/exllamav3/conversion/quant_config.py
@@ -8,12 +8,8 @@ def update_config(
     """
     Make necessary updates to config.json
     """
-    # The converter always writes a separate lm_head (quantized, on the device) next to the
-    # unquantized embedding table (in system memory), so a model that tied them in the source is
-    # untied in the output, and anything that trusts the flag (the transformers integration, other
-    # loaders) must see it that way. Our own loaders only tie when the lm_head tensor is absent
     if "tie_word_embeddings" in config_dict:
-        config_dict["tie_word_embeddings"] = False
+        config_dict["tie_word_embeddings"] = True
 
 
 def create_quantization_config_json(
